<article class="env-lemma" id="09YY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09YY">Lemma <span data-tag="09YY">32.9.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is finite, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S$ quasi-compact and quasi-separated. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $X$ is a directed limit $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X_ i$ where the transition maps are closed immersions and the objects $X_ i$ are finite and of finite presentation over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may write $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X_ i$ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/09ZQ" data-tag="09ZQ">32.9.5</a>. Applying Lemma <a href="/tag/09ZN" data-tag="09ZN">32.4.19</a> we see that $X_ i \to S$ is finite for large enough $i$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>